# Private host key for the klangk-ci VM (encrypted as
# klangk-ci-host-key.age via agenix). Mounting a *fixed* host key into the
# VM means wiping/rebuilding its disk does not rotate the key, so the
# github-runner-klangk.age secret never needs re-encrypting.
#
# Provisioning (one-time, already done - the plaintext key was fetched from
# the VM and placed at secrets/klangk-ci-host-key for encryption):
#   agenix -e secrets/klangk-ci-host-key.age   # paste secrets/klangk-ci-host-key contents
#   rm secrets/klangk-ci-host-key              # never keep the plaintext
#
# The VM mounts the decrypted key at
#   /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key (via klangk-ci.nix fileSystems)
#
# DO NOT COMMIT the plaintext key. Only the .age file is tracked.
klangk-ci-host-key
